adjudication.rationale:
The new API route `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts` gates access only by (1) `APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED` and (2) a header equality check:

```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  return res.status(403)
}
```

This check does not ensure the secret is configured/non-empty. If `CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is unset, `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is `undefined`, and a request with no such header yields `req.headers[...] === undefined`, so the comparison passes and the handler proceeds. Also, `.env.example` includes `CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""`; if a deployer leaves it empty, a request can satisfy the check by sending the header with an empty value.

After passing this gate, the handler trusts `userId` from the request body and updates/creates credentials for that user (`prisma.credential.update/create`), so bypassing the secret check enables arbitrary credential overwrite. The reachability depends on `APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED` (not shown), but the unsound auth check and its consequences are directly verifiable in the diff.
